    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0333" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.24/386a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Casablanca</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stanton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-30T16:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. Please urgently request Reed of Socony Vacuum<anchor n="45" xml:id="d268-f1"
                    /> to endeavor to check through his organization a report which has reached the
                    Department to the effect that under German pressure French authorities in
                    Tunisia have advanced for use of Axis forces in North Africa considerable
                    quantities of petroleum products, particularly from French naval reserve at
                    Bizerte, as well as a number of tanks and other equipment.</p>
                <p>The subject<anchor n="45a" xml:id="d268-f2"/> of the Department’s telegram No. 21
                    of January 29<anchor n="46" xml:id="d268-f3"/> might also be consulted in this
                    regard.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d268-f1" n="45" xml:id="d268-f1-content">
                <p>A. G. Reed, General Manager of the Socony-Vacuum Oil Company at Casablanca.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d268-f2" n="45a" xml:id="d268-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Robert A. Solborg, observer for the Military Intelligence Division, War
                    Department, in North Africa.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d268-f3" n="46" xml:id="d268-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
